<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Federico Ponce Vaides</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1889–1956</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Federico Ponce Vaides (1889–1956) was a Guatemalan general who became provisional president in July 1944 after protests forced the dictator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jorge-ubico">Jorge Ubico</a> to resign. When he tried to keep power through a managed election, a revolt by young officers, students and workers overthrew him on 20 October 1944, the start of the ten-year Guatemalan Revolution.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/federico-ponce-vaides.jpg" alt="Federico Ponce Vaides" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gobierno de Guatemala, Corte Suprema de Justicia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Federicoponcevaides_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
